---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { apps, href } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Install an app" description="How to add a web app to your Home Screen, with no app store.">
  <section class="wrap section narrow">
    <h1>Install an app</h1>
    <p class="lead">These apps open in your browser, and you can add each one to your device so it looks and works like any other app. There is no app store and nothing to download.</p>

    <h2>On an iPhone or iPad</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Open the app's link in <b>Safari</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap the <b>Share</b> button (the square with an arrow).</li>
      <li>Choose <b>Add to Home Screen</b>, then tap <b>Add</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted">On iPhone and iPad, only Safari can add an app to the Home Screen. Other browsers can use the app but not install it.</p>

    <h2>On an Android phone or tablet</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Open the app's link in <b>Chrome</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap the <b>⋮ menu</b>, then <b>Install app</b> (or <b>Add to Home screen</b>).</li>
      <li>Confirm. The app appears with your others.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>On a computer</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Open the app's link in <b>Chrome</b> or <b>Edge</b>.</li>
      <li>Click the <b>install</b> icon at the right of the address bar, or open the browser menu and choose <b>Install</b>.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Good to know</h2>
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li><b>Updates:</b> the app updates itself. When a new version is ready you will see a small "Update" prompt.</li>
      <li><b>Offline:</b> once it has opened once, it works without a connection. What you enter is saved on your device and syncs when you are back online.</li>
      <li><b>Your information:</b> on a device with no account, what you enter stays on that device. Clearing your browser's site data would remove it, so installing the app to your Home Screen is the safest way to keep it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Open an app</h2>
    <ul class="bullets">{apps.map((a) => <li><a href={a.appUrl}>{a.name}</a> · <a href={href(a.slug + '/')}>about it</a></li>)}</ul>
  </section>
</Base>
